---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import CopyBlock from "../components/CopyBlock.astro";
import { packs, REPO_URL, href } from "../lib/site";

const example = `id: console-x
name: "Console X launch lures"
version: 1
as_of: 2026-11-21
keywords: [console-x, "console x"]
intents: [download, free, key, keygen, crack, apk, pc, beta, early-access, generator]
brands:
  - {name: examplestore, official: [example.com]}
allowlist:
  outlets: [example.org]
  platforms: []
facts:
  as_of: 2026-11-21
  facts:
    - id: pc_release
      claim: "No PC version announced (replace with a dated, sourced claim)."
      status: not_announced
      as_of: 2026-11-21
      sources: [{url: "https://example.com/source", title: "Source", accessed: 2026-11-21}]
  platforms:
    pc: {status: unreleased, fact: pc_release, terms: [pc, windows, steam]}`;
---
<Base title="Campaign packs: add a launch in 20 lines" description="LureRadar campaign packs describe one hyped launch in YAML: keywords, intents, brands, allowlist and dated facts. GTA 6 ships first; add your own launch in about 20 lines." og="packs">
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Campaign packs" index="PCK" title="One engine," em="many launches.">
    <p>LureRadar is a generic launch-lure engine. Everything campaign-specific lives in a pack: keywords, lure intents, brands that scammers impersonate (names only, never logos), legitimate outlets, and dated, sourced facts that drive rules such as “there is no PC version yet”.</p>
  </PageHeader>
  <div class="wrap">
    {packs.length ? packs.map((p) => (
      <article class="card pack" data-reveal>
        <h2>{p.name} <span class="pill">{p.id} · v{p.version} · as of {p.as_of}</span></h2>
        <p class="muted">{p.description}</p>
        <div class="grid grid-2">
          <div><h3>Keywords</h3><p class="mono tags">{p.keywords.join(" · ")}</p></div>
          <div><h3>Impersonated brands</h3><ul>{p.brands.map((b: any) => <li>{b.name} <span class="muted mono">({b.official.join(", ")})</span></li>)}</ul></div>
          <div><h3>Platforms</h3><ul>{Object.entries(p.platforms).map(([k, v]: [string, any]) => <li>{v.label}: <span class={v.status === "unreleased" ? "warn" : "okc"}>{v.status}</span></li>)}</ul></div>
          <div><h3>Allowlist</h3><p>{p.allowlist_outlets} outlets (hard clear), {p.allowlist_platforms} user-content platforms (capped)</p></div>
        </div>
        <h3>Facts on record</h3>
        <ul class="facts">{p.facts.map((f: any) => <li><strong>{f.id}</strong> <span class="pill">{f.status}</span> <span class="muted">as of {f.as_of}</span><br />{f.claim} {f.sources.map((s: any) => <a href={s.url}>[{s.publisher ?? "source"}]</a>)}</li>)}</ul>
      </article>
    )) : <div class="empty"><strong>No packs loaded</strong>Pack data appears after <code>build_site_data.py</code> runs.</div>}
    <h2>Add a launch in about 20 lines</h2>
    <p>Scaffold with <code>lureradar pack new console-x</code>, edit, then run <code>lureradar pack validate</code>. Every fact needs a date and a source. Full format in the <a href={href("docs/packs/")}>pack documentation</a>; propose one with the <a href={`${REPO_URL}/issues/new?template=new-campaign-pack.yml`}>new campaign pack</a> form.</p>
    <CopyBlock text={example} label="Copy example pack" />
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  .pack { margin-top: 20px; }
  .pack h2 { margin-top: 0; display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; }
  .tags { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .warn { color: var(--amber); font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .okc { color: var(--radar); font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .facts { padding-left: 1.1em; display: grid; gap: 10px; }
</style>
